（长度 L+1），颜色仍为蓝(1)。若新线段超出网格列范围，超出部分不绘制。 3. 检查新线段的每个端点像素：若该像素位于网格第 0 行，则在第 0 行全行绘制红(2)（覆盖该行所有像素）；若位于末行，则在末行全行绘制红(2)；若位于第 0 列，则在第 0 列全列绘制红(2)；若位于末列，则在末列全列绘制红(2)。新绘制的红(2) 满条覆盖该行/列的所有先前内容（包括背景和蓝像素）。 4. 已存在的红(2) 满条各自向网格内部推进一格：顶边满条在第 1 行追加一行红(2)；底边满条在倒数第 2 行追加一行红(2)；左边满条在第 1 列追加一列红(2)；右边满条在倒数第 2 列追加一列红(2)。追加像素不覆盖蓝(1) 像素（蓝色优先）。 5. 多条线段按从左到右的顺序依次处理。  **关键洞察**：对角线段的推进是几何运动，边缘满条的生长是触发式扩展——两者通过"端点是否触及边缘"这一空间条件耦合。观察者必须同时追踪对角线段的落点和满条的扩展方向，才能正确推断输出。已有满条的向内推进是另一个隐蔽规则，需对比有/无已有满条的示例才能发现。  --- </new_puzzle>  ## 机制相似参考题  下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：优先使用新题中已经写明的原语、组合逻辑、来源原语和显式参考题 id；再用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。  已选参考：eval/21897d95, train/f0100645, train/465b7d93, train/337b420f, train/df978a02, eval/a251c730, train/54dc2872, train/e9fc42f2  新题正文显式提及的参考题 id：1b8318e3, 20fb2937, 21897d95, 337b420f, 465b7d93, 50c07299, 54dc2872, 60d73be6, 758abdf0, 83eb0a57, 84ba50d3, 8abad3cf, 984d8a3e, 9caf5b84, a251c730, abc82100, df978a02, e9fc42f2, f0100645, f931b4a8  文件头参考题组 id（弱提示）：none  <reference_puzzle rank="1" source="eval" puzzle_id="21897d95"> <similarity> score=1.0925 mechanism=1.0000 lexical=0.0127 code_feature=0.7500 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/21897d95.json </paths> <description> Repaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.  Input structure: - The grid is a mosaic of monochrome regions. - Color 1 forms T-shaped control markers on region boundaries. - Some controls use three singleton color-1 pixels around a colored center; that center is a literal replacement color. - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.  Rule: - For a color-1 T marker, the single stem points at the destination region to repaint. - The two diagonal cells behind the stem identify the source region; the destination gets that source region's original color. - For a colored-center T marker, the same stem identifies the destination, but the center color is the replacement. - All marker cells are filled with the final color of the source-side region. - A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.  Key insight: - The stem chooses what changes, while the two diagonals behind the stem choose where the marker itself belongs. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "transform_in_place",   "src": "monochrome regions with T-shaped color-1 control markers",   "transform": "recolor the region pointed to by each T stem using the original color from the two diagonal source cells behind the stem; colored-center T markers use the center color instead; erase marker cells into the source-side region",   "grid_shape": "same, except rotate 90 degrees when indicated by the colored-center control orientation",   "notes": "small non-rectangular colored scraps are absorbed into the neighboring region" } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  <reference_puzzle rank="2" source="train" puzzle_id="f0100645"> <similarity> score=1.0703 mechanism=1.0000 lexical=0.0084 code_feature=0.5714 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/f0100645.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/f0100645.json </paths> <description> Slide each inner colored object horizontally into the same-colored vertical wall until it touches an obstacle.  Input structure - The background is the dominant color. - The only foreground colors are two non-background colors. - One foreground color fills the left column and the other fills the right column. - Extra 8-connected objects of each wall color appear away from that color's wall.  Rule - Clear the extra objects from their original positions. - For each wall color, process its 8-connected extra objects from nearest to farthest from the matching wall. - Slide each object horizontally toward its matching wall as far as possible without overlapping the wall or an already settled object of the same color. - Keep the two vertical wall columns fixed.  Key insight - The side columns act like color-specific gravity walls: same-colored objects compact sideways against their own wall while preserving each object's shape. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "move_along_path",   "src": "8-connected objects away from the full-height side wall of the same color",   "path": "horizontal slide toward the matching side wall, stopping just before the wall or an already settled same-color object would overlap",   "trajectory": "translate each object rigidly to its final unobstructed position",   "transform": "clear original object positions, keep both side walls fixed, and preserve each moved object's color and shape",   "multi_step": "For each wall color, settle objects from nearest to farthest from that wall so later objects can stop against earlier same-color objects." } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  <reference_puzzle rank="3" source="train" puzzle_id="465b7d93"> <similarity> score=1.0646 mechanism=1.0000 lexical=0.0231 code_feature=0.5000 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/465b7d93.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/465b7d93.json </paths> <description> Move the small colored sprite into the hollow frame by stretching its shape to the frame interior.  Input structure: - The background is the dominant color. - There are exactly two foreground colors: one forms a complete rectangular   one-pixel-thick frame, and the other forms one 4-connected sprite outside it. - The frame interior is initially background.  Rule: - Clear the original sprite from its outside location. - Map the sprite bbox to the frame interior bbox, sending bbox extremes to   interior extremes. - Draw straight horizontal or vertical segments between mapped positions of   adjacent sprite pixels, then fill any enclosed background 