 L-bend lands on that control pixel. - Clear each moved sprite from its old position, clear its consumed control pixel,   then paste all translated sprites; sprites without a matching control stay put.  Key insight - The marker color pairs a sprite with its destination control, while the L-bend   gives the orientation-independent anchor cell to place on that destination. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "move_to_match",   "src": "marked L-shaped sprite s with one embedded marker pixel",   "dst": "isolated control pixel d",   "match_cond": "s.marker.color == d.color and d lies on the outer diagonal ray from s.L_bend through s.marker",   "transform": "translate s so s.L_bend lands on d; clear original s and consumed d; keep unmatched sprites and unrelated single pixels unchanged" } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  <reference_puzzle rank="8" source="train" puzzle_id="e9fc42f2"> <similarity> score=1.0627 mechanism=1.0000 lexical=0.0135 code_feature=0.5000 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e9fc42f2.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e9fc42f2.json </paths> <description> Assemble the foreground objects by docking equal-colored boundary markers edge-to-edge.  Input structure The grid has a dominant background color and several 4-connected multicolor foreground objects.  One foreground color is the body color; the less frequent foreground colors are boundary connector markers, and each marker color appears once as a free end or twice as a matched docking pair.  Rule Crop each foreground object to its bounding box and translate the objects so that the two occurrences of every paired connector color touch on their exposed boundary sides.  Preserve each object's orientation and colors, then return the tight crop around the assembled foreground on the original background color.  Key insight The colored marker pixels are ports: matching colors specify which objects must touch, and the marker's side of its object determines the direction of the translation. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "move_to_match",   "src": "4-connected foreground object sprite s with boundary connector markers",   "dst": "matching boundary connector marker d on another sprite",   "match_cond": "s.marker.color == d.marker.color and the two marker pixels have opposite exposed sides",   "transform": "translate sprites so each paired marker touches edge-to-edge; preserve sprite colors and orientation",   "grid_shape": "tight crop of the assembled foreground on the original background color" } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  ## 必读参考代码路径  执行前请至少快速阅读这些文件的 `main()` 和 `generate_input()`，重点看它们如何避免退化输入、如何随机放置对象、如何验证隐式假设：  - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/f0100645.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/465b7d93.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/337b420f.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/df978a02.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/a251c730.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/54dc2872.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e9fc42f2.py`  ## 公共参考工具箱  执行前还必须快速阅读 `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/solvers/arc_utils.py`。它是 ARC 公共工具箱，包含统一的 `(r, c)` 坐标约定、bbox、连通域、裁剪、几何变换、颜色和网格操作等公共实现。生成代码时优先参考或复用这些函数；若直接 import，请确保目标文件仍可被 `SourceFileLoader` 直接加载，自检命令能独立运行。  ## 实现要求  1. `main(grid)` 必须实现新题描述中的确定性转换规则，不能只识别 `generate_input()` 的固定模板。禁止不同的input网格输出相同的output网格。 2. `generate_input()` 必须随机生成多样样例，不能固定死。随机维度应覆盖：网格大小、对象数量、位置、颜色、方向、形状参数或关键分支。注意若描述中存在若干，需实现而不是只有单个，包括object或者对应关系等等。 3. 生成器必须保证输入满足 `main()` 的隐式假设：对象不重叠、不越界、特殊标记唯一或可区分、匹配关系无歧义、关键分支出现概率相同。 4. 禁止把 ARC 颜色 id 、亮度、拼写等当作人类不可见的数值语义参与排序、大小比较或隐藏映射。颜色变化必须有可见结构线索。注意颜色亮度、拼写等也是不可见信息，若描述中出现违规的颜色id或者亮度，可自行使用少量的固定颜色替代，但注意生成时要在三个以内输入输出网格中对所有变换100%覆盖度。 5. 输出样例要视觉清晰，人类必须能从输入输出对中肉眼辨认出规律。具体要求：避免对象粘连、覆盖关系混乱、同一像素多重语义；不同逻辑步骤产生的结果不要大面积层叠在一起导致无法分辨哪个颜色属于哪个步骤；输入中各元素之间保持足够间距，输出中新增的标记/填充/路径等应与背景和已有元素在颜色上有明显区分；若规则涉及多层叠加，生成时控制对象密度和尺寸，确保叠加区域只占少数像素而非铺满整个网格。 6. 若规则有多个分支，生成器不能长期固定成一个分支；应让分支